course: dictionary
lesson: 445
title: One word, three meanings: arctic
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Arctic has three meanings, and the sentence tells you which one you need. The Arctic is a place: the very cold area around the North Pole, with the Arctic Ocean and the northern parts of Canada, Alaska, Greenland, Norway and Russia. «Arctic foxes have small ears, short legs and short noses that lose little heat.» Here the word is used as an adjective, so it means from or about the Arctic.
explain: Sometimes Arctic is informal and means extremely cold. Ask yourself: is this sentence about a real place, or about the weather? «It was arctic inside the tent.» Nobody means the Arctic Ocean there; they mean it was freezing. Try your meaning in the sentence and see if it still makes sense.
explain: The Arctic is mostly a frozen ocean covered with sea ice. «Arctic sea ice is shrinking because the world is getting warmer.» Here the Arctic is a real place with real ice, and the sentence tells you that the ice is getting smaller.
fact: The Arctic is the very cold area around the North Pole.
fact: The Arctic is mostly a frozen ocean covered with sea ice.
fact: Arctic (adjective) means from or about the Arctic, as in Arctic foxes and Arctic terns.
fact: Arctic (informal) means extremely cold, as in «arctic weather».
fact: The Arctic Circle is an imaginary line around the Arctic.
exercise: «Arctic sea ice is shrinking because the world is getting warmer.» What is shrinking? | The desert | The sun | The polar bears | *Arctic sea ice
exercise: «It was arctic inside the tent.» What does arctic mean in this sentence? | Very loud | Hot and sticky | Dark and wet | *Extremely cold
exercise: «Arctic foxes have small ears, short legs and short noses.» Which word is an adjective here? | foxes | legs | *Arctic | small
test: «An Arctic fox mother can have over ten cubs in a good lemming year.» What is a cub? | *A baby fox | A small island | A lemming | A type of sea ice
test: The Arctic is mostly what kind of place? | A big city | A jungle | *A frozen ocean covered with sea ice | A desert
exam: Which phrase names an imaginary line around the Arctic? | Arctic fox | *Arctic Circle | Arctic tern | Arctic Ocean
